1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,293
OK. I'm here to walk you through what it takes

2
00:00:02,293 --> 00:00:04,170
to earn a single subject music credential

3
00:00:04,170 --> 00:00:04,879
in California,

4
00:00:04,879 --> 00:00:07,007
which authorizes you to teach music

5
00:00:07,007 --> 00:00:08,800
at any grade level, PK through 12.

6
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,136
To do that, you need a bachelor's degree,

7
00:00:11,136 --> 00:00:12,846
subject matter competency in music,

8
00:00:12,846 --> 00:00:14,848
and completion
of a credential program

9
00:00:14,848 --> 00:00:16,558
that includes a music methods course

10
00:00:16,558 --> 00:00:18,184
and student teaching.

11
00:00:18,184 --> 00:00:19,602
Subject matter competency

12
00:00:19,602 --> 00:00:21,021
simply means demonstrating

13
00:00:21,021 --> 00:00:22,230
that you know music.

14
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:23,273
Most candidates do that

15
00:00:23,273 --> 00:00:24,566
either through a music degree

16
00:00:24,566 --> 00:00:26,651
or by passing the CSET in music.

17
00:00:26,693 --> 00:00:27,861
If you're just starting out,

18
00:00:27,861 --> 00:00:29,696
the goal is to get that full
credential.

19
00:00:29,696 --> 00:00:31,406
And the earlier
you plan your coursework,

20
00:00:31,448 --> 00:00:33,283
the smoother that path will be.
